efully to avoid missing any critical information, as I'm aiming to have a reliable backup system in place! Let’s see what I find.\"}]}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_Nf9enSrw2Or0nZAXYEddhoq3|fc_00d03bd1c872351b0169d802a953408191ab32c24e3ee8971a","name":"read","arguments":{"file_path":"/home/node/.openclaw/skills/slm-expert-backup/SKILL.md"},"partialJson":"{\"file_path\":\"/home/node/.openclaw/skills/slm-expert-backup/SKILL.md\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_QzzGI3hSxs0zwgL5H8l0oN7p|fc_00d03bd1c872351b0169d802a9534c8191ae07e125db6c66aa","name":"read","arguments":{"file_path":"/home/node/.openclaw/skills/slm-dermatology/references/prompt-template.md"},"partialJson":"{\"file_path\":\"/home/node/.openclaw/skills/slm-dermatology/references/prompt-template.md\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_XQGPF0RAhnY3cAHnClToIDAx|fc_00d03bd1c872351b0169d802a95354819187abdf977d2dbcfc","name":"read","arguments":{"file_path":"/home/node/.openclaw/skills/slm-expert-backup/references/prompt-template.md"},"partialJson":"{\"file_path\":\"/home/node/.openclaw/skills/slm-expert-backup/references/prompt-template.md\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_xZ360VE9fZc5gG64s1BuQIqW|fc_00d03bd1c872351b0169d802a953588191bee7938d0ded4777","name":"read","arguments":{"file_path":"/home/node/.openclaw/skills/slm-dermatology/scripts/query_slm_dermatology.py"},"partialJson":"{\"file_path\":\"/home/node/.openclaw/skills/slm-dermatology/scripts/query_slm_dermatology.py\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_Azx8QY4jEgYtUxTJeUAnZPdG|fc_00d03bd1c872351b0169d802a9535c81919d492c51490de839","name":"read","arguments":{"file_path":"/home/node/.openclaw/skills/slm-expert-backup/scripts/query_slm_expert_backup.py"},"partialJson":"{\"file_path\":\"/home/node/.openclaw/skills/slm-expert-backup/scripts/query_slm_expert_backup.py\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":1130,"output":206,"cacheRead":14720,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":16056,"cost":{"input":0.0028250000000000003,"output":0.00309,"cacheRead":0.0036799999999999997,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.009595}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1775764132522}}
{"type":"message","id":"4820d7e7","parentId":"af68fff5","timestamp":"2026-04-09T19:48:57.470Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_Nf9enSrw2Or0nZAXYEddhoq3|fc_00d03bd1c872351b0169d802a953408191ab32c24e3ee8971a","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"---\nname: slm-expert-backup\ndescription: Query a backup small language model (SLM) endpoint with expertise in nephrology, hypertension, and cardiology by asking a focused question grounded in retrieved records or clearly established conversation context, then processing the answer in the calling agent. Use when the agent needs a compact specialty model pass for kidney, blood-pressure, or cardiovascular interpretation, follow-up reasoning, or record-grounded support, and does not need any adapter-loading step before inference.\n---\n\n# SLM Expert Backup\n\nUse this skill to ask the backup specialty SLM a focused question about nephrology, hypertension, or cardiology context, then process the answer in the calling agent.\n\n## Workflow\n\n1. Confirm the task is within scope.\n   - Use this skill for nephrology, hypertension, or cardiology interpretation, summarization, pattern spotting, follow-up reasoning, or record-grounded specialty questions.\n   - Prefer this skill when the user’s question concerns kidney disease, CKD, AKI, proteinuria, electrolytes, blood-pressure management, hypertensive organ damage, cardiovascular disease, cardiac risk, or cardiology follow-up.\n   - Do not use it for unrelated specialties.\n\n2. Build a focused question for the SLM.\n   - Write a single clear specialty question.\n   - Ground the question in retrieved records or clearly stated conversation facts.\n   - Keep it concise and specific.\n   - Do not invent findings, diagnoses, timelines, or test results.\n   - Good examples:\n     - `Based on this kidney-history summary, which findings most strongly support CKD progression and what follow-up should be prioritized?`\n     - `From this hypertension history, which missing details would matter most before judging whether control is adequate?`\n     - `Given these cardiovascular risk factors and symptoms, what cardiology-focused concerns deserve the closest follow-up?`\n     - `What nephrology and hypertension features best explain worsening renal function in this blood-pressure context?`\n\n3. Choose the specialty domain routing.\n   - Always send one or more domains with the question.\n   - Use only these values: `nephrology`, `hypertension`, `cardiology`.\n   - Choose the narrowest correct set.\n   - Use multiple domains only when the question genuinely spans them.\n   - Example mappings:\n     - CKD, AKI, proteinuria, renal imaging, electrolyte or acid-base questions -> `nephrology`\n     - Blood pressure control, resistant hypertension, antihypertensive strategy, hypertensive organ damage -> `hypertension`\n     - Cardiac symptoms, heart failure, ischemic risk, lipid or cardiovascular-risk questions -> `cardiology`\n     - Hypertensive kidney damage -> `nephrology`, `hypertension`\n     - Cardiorenal questions -> `nephrology`, `cardiology`\n\n4. Query the backup SLM without loading any adapter.\n   - Do not perform any adapter-load step.\n   - Run:\n\n```bash\npython3 scripts/query_slm_expert_backup.py \\\n  --question \"What signs of kidney damage should be monitored in hypertensive patients?\" \\\n  --domain nephrology \\\n  --domain hypertension\n```\n\n   - The script sends this payload shape:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"question\": \"string\",\n  \"domains\": [\"string\"]\n}\n```\n\n   - Endpoint:\n\n```text\nhttp://looporchestra.sytes.net:8008/query\n```\n\n5. Read the response.\n   - Prefer a clean text answer.\n   - Accept common shapes such as `answer`, `Answer`, `response`, `message`, or raw text.\n   - If the endpoint returns nested JSON encoded as a string, extract the useful answer text when possible.\n   - If parsing is ambiguous, keep the best raw text and say so briefly in your own reasoning.\n   - If the answer is `Not found in context.`, report that plainly instead of inventing content.\n\n6. Process the SLM answer in the calling agent.\n   - Do not treat the SLM output as the final user-facing answer by default.\n   - Use it as an input to the agent’s own reasoning, synthesis, or explanation.\n   - Cross-check it against the actual record or conversation context already available.\n   - Preserve uncertainty and avoid overstating confidence.\n   - If clinically relevant, highlight missing nephrology, hypertension, or cardiology history, red flags, or next-step questions.\n   - Treat the output as supportive specialty inference, not as a confirmed diagnosis.\n\n## Output pattern\n\nReturn a response that includes:\n\n- **SLM finding**: the key content from the model answer, cleaned up if needed\n- **Domain(s)**: the domains used for the query\n- **Agent interpretation**: the calling agent’s processed interpretation grounded in the available context\n- **Cautions / next steps**: only when relevant\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1775764137467}}
{"type":"message","id":"5bbb4c7c","parentId":"4820d7e7","timestamp":"2026-04-09T19:48:57.477Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_QzzGI3hSxs0zwgL5H8l0oN7p|fc_00d03bd1c872351b0169d802a9534c8191ae07e125db6c66aa","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Dermatology SLM question template\n\nUse this shape when turning retrieved patient records, lesion descriptions, rash history, or already-established image context into one focused dermatology question for the SLM.\n\n```text\nPatient / dermatology context:\n- Patient id: <known or omitted>\n- Main skin concern: <known facts only>\n- Lesion / rash description: <known morphology, distribution, duration, symptoms>\n- Relevant history / treatments / triggers / images: <known facts only>\n- Important uncertainties or missing data: <if relevant>\n\nQuestion for SLM:\n<one clear dermatology question grounded in the available context>\n```\n\nGuidance:\n- Keep the final question focused and answerable.\n- Base it only on retrieved records or clearly stated conversation context.\n- Do not invent morphology, diagnoses, timing, or response-to-treatment details.\n- Prefer one strong dermatology question over several weak ones.\n- The calling agent should interpret the returned answer instead of relaying it blindly.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1775764137475}}
{"type":"message","id":"589c62b1","parentId":"5bbb4c7c","timestamp":"2026-04-09T19:48:57.482Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_XQGPF0RAhnY3cAHnClToIDAx|fc_00d03bd1c872351b0169d802a95354819187abdf977d2dbcfc","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Backup specialty SLM question template\n\nUse this shape when turning retrieved patient records or clearly established nephrology, hypertension, or cardiology context into one focused specialty question for the backup SLM.\n\n```text\nPatient / specialty context:\n- Patient id: <known or omitted>\n- Main concern: <known facts only>\n- Relevant kidney / blood pressure / cardiovascular findings: <known facts only>\n- Relevant history / medications / labs / imaging: <known facts only>\n- Important uncertainties or missing data: <if relevant>\n\nQuestion for SLM:\n<one clear specialty question grounded in the available context>\n```\n\nGuidance:\n- Keep the final question focused and answerable.\n- Base it only on retrieved records or clearly stated conversation context.\n- Do not invent diagnoses, test results, timing, or treatment response.\n- Prefer one strong specialty question over several weak ones.\n- The calling agent should interpret the returned answer instead of relaying it blindly.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1775764137480}}
{"type":"message","id":"cc2fd7a3","parentId":"589c62b1","timestamp":"2026-04-09T19:48:57.487Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_xZ360VE9fZc5gG64s1BuQIqW|fc_00d03bd1c872351b0169d802a953588191bee7938d0ded4777","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"#!/usr/bin/env python3\nimport argparse\nimport json\nimport sys\nfrom urllib import error, request\n\nBASE_URL = \"http://looporchestra.sytes.net:8007\"\nLOAD_ADAPTER_ENDPOINT = f\"{BASE_URL}/node/load-adapter\"\nCHAT_ENDPOINT = f\"{BASE_URL}/chat\"\nLOAD_ADAPTER_PAYLOAD = {\n    \"model\": \"tinyllama\",\n    \"adapter_path\": \"adapters/derma_v1.0\",\n    \"mode\": \"derma\",\n}\n\n\ndef extract_answer(body: str) -> str:\n    try:\n        parsed = json.loads(body)\n    except json.JSONDecodeError:\n        return body.strip()\n\n    if isinstance(parsed, str):\n        return parsed.strip()\n\n    if not isinstance(parsed, dict):\n        return json.dumps(parsed, indent=2)\n\n    for key in (\"answer\", \"Answer\", \"response\", \"message\"):\n        value = parsed.get(key)\n        if value is not None:\n            if isinstance(value, str):\n                text = value.strip()\n                try:\n                    nested = json.loads(text)\n                    if isinstance(nested, dict):\n                        for nested_key in (\"answer\", \"Answer\", \"response\", \"message\"):\n                            nested_value = nested.get(nested_key)\n                            if nested_value is not None:\n                                return str(nested_value).strip()\n                except json.JSONDecodeError:\n                    pass\n                return text\n            return json.dumps(value, indent=2)\n\n    data = parsed.get(\"data\")\n    if isinstance(data, dict):\n        for key in (\"answer\", \"Answer\", \"response\", \"message\"):\n            value = data.get(key)\n            if value is not None:\n                return value if isinstance(value, str) else json.dumps(value, indent=2)\n\n    return json.dumps(parsed, indent=2)\n\n\ndef post_json(url: str, payload: dict, timeout: int) -> str:\n    req = request.Request(\n        url,\n        data=json.dumps(payload).encode(\"utf-8\"),\n        headers={\"Content-Type\": \"application/json\", \"Accept\": \"application/json\"},\n        method=\"POST\",\n    )\n\n    try:\n        with request.urlopen(req, timeout=timeout) as resp:\n            return resp.read().decode(\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\")\n    except error.HTTPError as e:\n        detail = e.read().decode(\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\")\n        raise RuntimeError(f\"HTTP {e.code} from {url}: {detail}\") from e\n    except Exception as e:\n        raise RuntimeError(f\"Request to {url} failed: {e}\") from e\n\n\ndef load_adapter(timeout: int) -> str:\n    return post_json(LOAD_ADAPTER_ENDPOINT, LOAD_ADAPTER_PAYLOAD, timeout)\n\n\ndef call_endpoint(question: str, timeout: int = 45) -> str:\n    load_adapter(timeout)\n    body = post_json(CHAT_ENDPOINT, {\"question\": question}, timeout)\n    return extract_answer(body)\n\n\ndef main():\n    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(\n        description=\"Load the dermatology adapter and query the dermatology SLM endpoint\"\n    )\n    parser.add_argument(\"question\", help=\"Dermatology question grounded in records or known context\")\n    parser.add_argument(\"--timeout\", type=int, default=45)\n    args = parser.parse_args()\n\n    answer = call_endpoint(args.question, timeout=args.timeout)\n    print(answer)\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    try:\n        main()\n    except Exception as exc:\n        print(f\"ERROR: {exc}\", file=sys.stderr)\n        sys.exit(1)\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1775764137485}}
{"type":"message","id":"53cc76b2","parentId":"cc2fd7a3","timestamp":"2026-04-09T19:48:57.494Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_Azx8QY4jEgYtUxTJeUAnZPdG|fc_00d03bd1c872351b0169d802a9535c81919d492c51490de839","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"#!/usr/bin/env python3\nimport argparse\nimport json\nimport sys\nfrom urllib import error, request\n\nQUERY_ENDPOINT = \"http://looporchestra.sytes.net:8008/query\"\nALLOWED_DOMAINS = {\"nephrology\", \"hypertension\", \"cardiology\"}\n\n\ndef extract_answer(body: str) -> str:\n    try:\n        parsed = json.loads(body)\n    except json.JSONDecodeError:\n        return body.strip()\n\n    if isinstance(parsed, str):\n        return parsed.strip()\n\n    if not isinstance(parsed, dict):\n        return json.dumps(parsed, indent=2)\n\n    for key in (\"answer\", \"Answer\", \"response\", \"message\"):\n        value = parsed.get(key)\n        if value is not None:\n            if isinstance(value, str):\n                text = value.strip()\n                try:\n                    nested = json.loads(text)\n                    if isinstance(nested, dict):\n                        for nested_key in (\"answer\", \"Answer\", \"response\", \"message\"):\n                            nested_value = nested.get(nested_key)\n                            if nested_value is not None:\n                                return str(nested_value).strip()\n                except json.JSONDecodeError:\n                    pass\n                return text\n            return json.dumps(value, indent=2)\n\n    data = parsed.get(\"data\")\n    if isinstance(data, dict):\n        for key in (\"answer\", \"Answer\", \"response\", \"message\"):\n            value = data.get(key)\n            if value is not None:\n                return value if isinstance(value, str) else json.dumps(value, indent=2)\n\n    return json.dumps(parsed, indent=2)\n\n\ndef post_json(url: str, payload: dict, timeout: int) -> str:\n    req = request.Request(\n        url,\n        data=json.dumps(payload).encode(\"utf-8\"),\n        headers={\"Content-Type\": \"application/json\", \"Accept\": \"application/json\"},\n        method=\"POST\",\n    )\n\n    try:\n        with request.urlopen(req, timeout=timeout) as resp:\n            return resp.read().decode(\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\")\n    except error.HTTPError as e:\n        detail = e.read().decode(\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\")\n        raise RuntimeError(f\"HTTP {e.code} from {url}: {detail}\") from e\n    except Exception as e:\n        raise RuntimeError(f\"Request to {url} failed: {e}\") from e\n\n\ndef call_endpoint(question: str, timeout: int = 45) -> str:\n    body = post_json(QUERY_ENDPOINT, {\"question\": question}, timeout)\n    return extract_answer(body)\n\n\ndef main():\n    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(\n        description=\"Query the backup SLM chat endpoint with a single question payload\"\n    )\n    parser.add_argument(\"--question\", required=True, help=\"Question to send to the chat endpoint\")\n    parser.add_argument(\"--timeout\", type=int, default=45)\n    args = parser.parse_args()\n\n    answer = call_endpoint(args.question, timeout=args.timeout)\n    print(answer)\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    try:\n        main()\n    except Exception as exc:\n        print(f\"ERROR: {exc}\", file=sys.stderr)\n        sys.exit(1)\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1775764137491}}
